From: EglantinePS5
Subject: [PATCH] up: making the shader list before play tells the boot screen and the log how far it is (reading, making, saving), through a hook the front sets

Switch: none of its own; only while the front has set the hook, which it does only with
EDEN_UP_SHADER_SET_PREPASS=1 (0770, off by default) and only around LoadDiskResources.

Why: in run1382 (13 Nov, T162) the boot screen showed "2594/2594" (the boot pipelines) and then
nothing moved for about 12 minutes while the shader list was made and saved, and the log had
nothing between 71 s and 738 s. The owner wants the progress shown.

This is T165a's 0832 (branch t165a) without its vk_pipeline_cache.cpp part. That file is one of
the files the translation id (tools/gen-translation-id.py, <build>/vk_pipeline_cache_cost.cpp) is
made of, and with EDEN_UP_SHADER_PREP_SOURCE_STAMP=1 the prepared store's stamp and the shader
set's stamp carry that id: any change to it gives a new, empty store and makes the shader list
again (12 minutes in run1382). Our console is filling T162's store now, so T165 keeps the
id: this patch changes only shader_set.cpp/.h, the new shader_set_progress.h and
nx2_shader_extract.h, none of which the id reads. 0831 (the time limit from when preparing starts) is left out of T165 for the same reason.

What:
- ShaderSet::Prepare takes an optional OnProgress (Part::Files / Records / Save, done, total):
  called when a part begins, about twice a second while it runs, and at its end. Never called
  when the file is reused (its stamp holds).
- shader_set_progress.h holds Part, OnProgress and SetBootProgress, so the front can include it
  without shader_set.h (which brings in the engine headers; the front builds with -Werror and
  the port's macro.h fails there).
- ShaderSet::SetBootProgress(hook): the front's hook. While it is set, a Prepare called without
  OnProgress (the before-play pass calls it so) sends its parts there; it is called under a mutex,
  so a hook cleared with SetBootProgress({}) is never called again.
- With either, Prepare logs one line every 10 s per part in one format: "Shader set before play:
  <part>: <done> of <total> <unit> (<n>%), <rate> a second, about <m> min left; <s> s; <MB> MB
  free memory" (the free memory is there to show next time whether the slow save of run1382 went
  with little free memory; not checked). The extractor's own 10 s "extracting:" line is replaced
  by it then.
- The extractor's progress interval (Nx2ShaderExtract::Progress::every) is in milliseconds now
  (500 ms with a hook, 10 s as before without; its loop checks every 250 ms).

Not here (they need vk_pipeline_cache.cpp): the count of the list's keys (12.5 s in run1382) gets
no counter (the screen keeps the saving part at 100% meanwhile), and the preparing line keeps its
old format. Hook not set: nothing changes. Not checked: a run, a build.
---
